// MENUDEF - the mod's own menu. ZDoom wiki: https://zdoom.org/wiki/MENUDEF
//
// A MENUDEF lump does not replace GZDoom's menus; it adds to them. The two
// directives used here:
//
//   OptionMenu "<name>"       declares a new menu screen.
//   AddOptionMenu "<name>"    APPENDS items to a menu that already exists,
//                             leaving the rest of the engine's menu intact.
//                             (GZDoom's own option menus are declared
//                             `protected`, which forbids a mod from adding
//                             Command/SafeCommand items - arbitrary console
//                             commands - but allows Submenu, Option and
//                             StaticText. Verified in-engine 2026-10-13.)
//
// WHY THERE IS NO CVAR OF OUR OWN FOR THE LANGUAGE.
// GZDoom already ships the `language` CVar, and it is archived: the engine
// writes it to the player's gzdoom.ini and reads it back next launch. That
// is exactly the persistence the CEO asked for, in the place a player
// expects their settings to live, and it is the ONLY key this mod ever
// touches in their config. A mod-owned CVar would be a second source of
// truth and a second thing written to their file.
// See docs/engine/adr/004-language-switch-and-difficulty-ladder.md.

// The four values GZDoom's `language` CVar can hold in this mod.
// "default" is GZDoom's code for the LANGUAGE section marked `default`
// (ours is `[enu default]`); "ru" selects `[ru]`; "ca" selects `[ca]`
// (Catalan, D97, P6: GZDoom ships no Catalan of its own, so the engine's
// own menus stay English while the mod's text is Catalan); "auto" is the engine's
// own "ask the operating system", and it is the value in every config that
// has never been touched.
//
// WHY "auto" IS IN THE LIST (it was not, until 2026-10-13 - bug E3).
// An OptionString row whose CVar holds a value absent from its list has
// nothing to show and GZDoom draws "Unknown"
// (gzdoom.pk3:zscript/engine/ui/menu/optionmenuitems.zs). The mod used to
// hide that by having a ZScript OptionMenu subclass overwrite "auto" with
// the code auto had already resolved to. That subclass is gone and this
// row is the reason why:
//
//   GZDoom allows ZScript to write a CVar ONLY while the engine is
//   handling menu INPUT. In 4.14.2 `DMenu::InMenu` is raised around
//   exactly three calls - OnUIEvent, OnInputEvent and MenuEvent
//   (src/common/menu/menu.cpp:276-327) - and around nothing else. Init,
//   Ticker and Drawer all run with InMenu == 0, and a CVar write from
//   there aborts the VM with "Attempt to change CVAR 'language' outside
//   of menu code". Verified in-engine 2026-10-13 from BOTH hooks.
//   Opening this screen the ordinary way happened to survive only because
//   the submenu is built inside the PARENT menu's MenuEvent; `openmenu
//   SD_OptionsMenu` from the console, or a key bound to it, killed the
//   game. See docs/engine/adr/004-language-switch-and-difficulty-ladder.md.
//
// Declaring the value costs one line and writes nothing, so there is no
// longer any code of ours that can abort. Choosing English, Russian or
// Catalan still writes the CVar - but through the engine's own Option row, during
// input handling, where it is legal - and the engine archives it.
//
// The labels are localized like everything else, so the Russian build names
// the languages in Russian. They are not endonyms ("Русский" inside the
// English menu): when this was written Freedoom's font could not draw
// Cyrillic (debt T9, paid by D24 on 2026-10-13 with the mod's own glyphs).
// Now that it can, endonyms are a product choice, not this lump's.
//
// `OptionString`, NOT `OptionValue`. GZDoom has two list directives and they
// differ by the CVar's TYPE: OptionValue parses its left column as a NUMBER,
// OptionString as a string. `language` is a string CVar, so the OptionValue
// form is a parse error. It is not a soft one either - verified in-engine on
// 2026-10-13, GZDoom 4.14.2 aborts during startup (exit 255, the log stops
// at "M_Init: Init menus.") and the mod never reaches the title screen. The
// whole game fails to launch over one keyword, so do not "simplify" this.

OptionString "SD_LanguageValues"
{
	"auto",    "$SD_LANGVAL_AUTO"
	"default", "$SD_LANGVAL_EN"
	"ru",      "$SD_LANGVAL_RU"
	"ca",      "$SD_LANGVAL_CA"
}

// --- The menu font ----------------------------------------------------------
// D31 (CEO, 2026-10-13): the main menu and the skill screen are TEXT in our
// own alphabet, not Freedoom's pictures of English words (debt T12).
// docs/engine/MOD-SPEC.md 6.6 is the contract; the reasoning is
// docs/engine/adr/005-menu-text-instead-of-menu-graphics.md.
//
// "SDMENU" is the folder font fonts/sdmenu/ (art-director, built by
// tools/art/gen_menu.py): bigfont with five Latin capitals drawn as Cyrillic
// letters, D22 level 2 - R as Я, N as И, E as Э, W as Ш, A as Д. ONE font
// serves both languages: the [ru] strings are written in Cyrillic code
// points, which the font leaves alone, so English reads "ИЭШ GДMЭ" and
// Russian reads as Russian. Nothing below is per-language.
//
// Why not BigFont: the menu code swaps SmallFont and BigFont for their
// "alternative" versions by itself (menuDelegate.PickFont,
// gzdoom.pk3:zscript/engine/ui/menu/menucustomize.zs:25), and D22 must not
// reach the level names and pickups BigFont prints. A font with its own
// name is drawn as named.
//
// Colours: "Cream" for an item, "Gold" for the selected one (art-director's
// proposal). The glyphs are drawn red; untranslated they would be red on
// TITLEPIC's red. Both are engine colour names (gzdoom.pk3:textcolors.txt).
//
// The strings are in CAPITALS in LANGUAGE because the font has no
// lowercase; what GZDoom does with lowercase in a capitals-only folder font
// is NOT VERIFIED for this one.
//
// If fonts/sdmenu/ is missing from the PK3, tools/check_pk3.py fails the
// package (category "menus").

// --- The episode menu (D41) -------------------------------------------------
// The weapons test range (map RANGE since D62) ships as a practice range: a second MAPINFO
// episode. With one episode the engine autoselected it and this screen never
// showed; with two, New Game -> this screen -> the skill screen. The engine's
// own body (gzdoom.pk3:menudef.txt, ListMenu "EpisodeMenu", IfGame(Doom)):
//     NetgameMessage "$NEWGAME"
//     Position 48, 63
//     StaticPatch 54, 38, "M_EPISOD", 0 , "$MNU_EPISODE"
//     linespacing 16
// M_EPISOD is Freedoom's picture of "Which episode?" in English (debt T12),
// so the screen is redeclared exactly like the skill screen below, and for
// the same reason in the same order: the logo, ONE header in SDMENU, then
// SmallFont LAST, because the engine appends one text item per episode at
// run time in the font the descriptor ends with (M_StartupEpisodeMenu, engine
// source). The episode names are proper nouns under D22, so they are drawn
// in SmallFont like the skill names, not in SDMENU. NetgameMessage is kept:
// it is what refuses New Game during a net game.
// Contract: docs/engine/MOD-SPEC.md 4.4 and 6.6; the choice of an episode
// over a main-menu item: docs/engine/adr/007-practice-range-as-a-second-episode.md.
// Re-diff against gzdoom.pk3/menudef.txt on an engine upgrade - debt T14.
LISTMENU "EpisodeMenu"
{
	NetgameMessage "$NEWGAME"
	StaticPatch 60, 0, "M_DOOM"
	Font "SDMENU", "Cream"
	StaticText 32, 70, "$SD_MNU_CHOOSEEPISODE"
	Font "SmallFont", "Red", "Gold"
	LineSpacing 12
	Position 32, 90
}

// --- The difficulty menu --------------------------------------------------
// BUG E4, found in-engine 2026-10-13: the fifth rung, "Hero of the Soviet
// Union, posthumously", ran off the right edge of the screen and read
// "HERO OF THE SOVIET UNION, POSTHU". The name is the CEO's and is not the
// thing to change (docs/product/DIFFICULTY-NAMES.md owns it); the font is.
// The rungs are drawn in SmallFont, red with a gold highlight (D-004-1).
//
// THE ORDER OF THE TWO `Font` LINES IS LOAD-BEARING. A static item takes the
// descriptor's font when it is parsed (ListMenuItemStaticText.Init,
// gzdoom.pk3:zscript/engine/ui/menu/listmenuitems.zs:158-165). The five
// rungs are NOT listed here: the engine builds them at run time from
// MAPINFO's `skill` blocks, in whatever font the descriptor ENDS with. So
// SDMENU first, for the header, and SmallFont last, for the rungs. The
// engine's own "PlayerMenu" does the same: a header, then Font "SmallFont"
// (gzdoom.pk3:menudef.txt:458-459).
//
// LAYOUT (D31, art-director's sheet
// docs/art/previews/2026-10-13_1554_F2_menu-sweep.png). The engine draws two
// headers, M_NEWG at (96,14) and M_SKILL at (54,38); both land on the name
// painted into TITLEPIC (docs/qa/evidence/2026-10-13_0955_F2_skill-ladder-en.png).
// Here the logo stays where the title screen has it - the same 60,0 as the
// main menu - and ONE header sits under it. "New Game" is not repeated: the
// player has just chosen it.
//
// x = 32 FOR THE RUNGS. Rung 5 is 288 px in fonts/defsmallfont/, so 32 is
// the largest x that keeps it on a 320-wide screen (32 + 288 = 320); the
// skull selector is drawn 32 px left of the rungs (Doom's
// Selector "M_SKULL1", -32, -5), so 32 is also the smallest x that keeps it
// on a 4:3 screen. At the old x = 48 the engine moved the rungs itself, to
// about x = 0 in the 0955 screenshot, and the skull left the 4:3 area; the
// rule it applied is NOT VERIFIED, and at 32 it has nothing to correct.
// tests/test_menudef.py re-measures this whenever a name or the font
// changes.
//
// A redeclared LISTMENU replaces the engine's descriptor, so leaving a line
// out deletes it. Re-diff against gzdoom.pk3/menudef.txt, ListMenu
// "SkillMenu", on an engine upgrade - debt T14.
LISTMENU "SkillMenu"
{
	StaticPatch 60, 0, "M_DOOM"
	Font "SDMENU", "Cream"
	StaticText 32, 70, "$SD_MNU_CHOOSESKILL"
	Font "SmallFont", "Red", "Gold"
	LineSpacing 12
	Position 32, 90
}

// --- The main menu ----------------------------------------------------------
// BUG E1 (found by the CEO on docs/qa/evidence/2026-10-13_0100_F2_title-and-menu.png):
// on the title screen the menu's M_DOOM block did not land on the name block
// painted into TITLEPIC, and a "CO" of the latter showed past its left edge.
//
// It was this lump's fault, not the art's. `art-director` generates both
// images from one lockup; where the loose copy belongs is the contract row
// in docs/engine/MOD-SPEC.md 6.6: M_DOOM goes at x=60, y=0 of the 320x200
// screen. Measured 2026-10-13: overlaying assets/graphics/shell/M_DOOM.png
// on TITLEPIC.png at (60,0) gives a mean per-channel difference of 6, and
// 22 or more at every neighbouring offset - so the art is exact and the
// contract is right. (The generator's manifest under gitignored work/ is
// evidence only; it is not in every clone.)
//
// GZDoom, however, was never told. Its own gzdoom.pk3/menudef.txt declares
//     LISTMENU "MainMenu" { ... StaticPatch 94, 2, "M_DOOM" ... }
// and a mod that ships no MainMenu of its own inherits those numbers: the
// logo was drawn 34 px right and 2 px down of where it was drawn into
// TITLEPIC.
//
// WHY THE WHOLE MENU IS REPEATED. There is no "move that item" directive:
// ADDLISTMENU only APPENDS, which here would draw a SECOND logo and leave
// the misplaced one in place. Redeclaring a LISTMENU replaces the engine's
// descriptor outright (verified in-engine 2026-10-13: five items, not ten),
// so every item has to be restated. The body below is GZDoom 4.14.2's own
// IfGame(Doom) branch with two changes: the logo's position, and (D31) each
// Freedoom `PatchItem "M_xxx"` turned into a `TextItem` reading LANGUAGE,
// with the same hotkey and the same target menu. The IfOption tests are
// kept, so a player's "swap menu" and "show ReadThis" settings keep working.
// Re-diff against gzdoom.pk3/menudef.txt when the engine is upgraded (T14).
//
// TextItem syntax is the engine's own: gzdoom.pk3:menudef.txt:129-137
// (LISTMENU "MainMenuTextOnly", e.g. TextItem "$MNU_NEWGAME", "n",
// "PlayerclassMenu") and :98-102 (the Heretic/Hexen main menu).
//
// The engine also ships that "MainMenuTextOnly" for localized content and
// can switch to it on its own; when it does is NOT VERIFIED. The Russian
// main menu (docs/qa/evidence/2026-10-13_1007_F2_mainmenu-ru.png) drew THIS
// menu, logo at 60,0, so today it does not. If the Russian capture ever
// shows the engine's strings and the logo at 94,2, redeclare
// "MainMenuTextOnly" with this same body.
LISTMENU "MainMenu"
{
	Font "SDMENU", "Cream", "Gold"
	LineSpacing 16
	StaticPatch 60, 0, "M_DOOM"
	Position 97, 72
	IfOption(ReadThis)
	{
		Position 97, 64
	}

	TextItem "$SD_MNU_NEWGAME", "n", "PlayerclassMenu"
	IfOption(SwapMenu)
	{
		TextItem "$SD_MNU_LOADGAME", "l", "LoadGameMenu"
		TextItem "$SD_MNU_SAVEGAME", "s", "SaveGameMenu"
		TextItem "$SD_MNU_OPTIONS", "o", "OptionsMenu"
	}
	else
	{
		TextItem "$SD_MNU_OPTIONS", "o", "OptionsMenu"
		TextItem "$SD_MNU_LOADGAME", "l", "LoadGameMenu"
		TextItem "$SD_MNU_SAVEGAME", "s", "SaveGameMenu"
	}
	IfOption(ReadThis)
	{
		TextItem "$SD_MNU_READTHIS", "r", "ReadThisMenu"
	}
	TextItem "$SD_MNU_QUITGAME", "q", "QuitMenu"
}

OptionMenu "SD_OptionsMenu"
{
	Title "$SD_OPTMNU_TITLE"
	// SDLanguageOption = the engine's Option row that also names "eng",
	// "enu", "rus"... instead of "Unknown" (bug QA-G6-1). It only READS
	// the CVar; src/zscript/sd/language_option.zs says why that matters.
	SDLanguageOption "$SD_OPTMNU_LANGUAGE", "language", "SD_LanguageValues"
	StaticText " "
	StaticText "$SD_OPTMNU_LANGHELP"
	StaticText " "
	Submenu "$SD_CRED_TITLE", "SD_CreditsMenu"
}

// --- Credits (G6) -------------------------------------------------------------
// The in-game credits: Options -> Soviet Doom -> Credits. The reasoning, and
// the options it was chosen against (a main-menu item, the F1 help pages,
// a text screen after the ending), are in
// docs/engine/adr/009-in-game-credits.md; the contract is
// docs/engine/MOD-SPEC.md 6.8.
//
// WHY AN OPTION MENU. The main menu, the skill screen and the episode screen
// are the CEO's approved text menu (D31/D32); a new row there changes what
// he approved. Our own option screen above already exists, so the credits
// cost one row on a screen of ours and nothing on his. An option menu also
// suits the text: every StaticText row is centred (OptionMenuItem.drawLabel,
// gzdoom.pk3:zscript/engine/ui/menu/optionmenuitems.zs:56-66) and drawn in
// the engine's NewSmallFont (Menu.OptionFont, menu.zs:346-349), which has
// Cyrillic of its own, so both languages print without our alphabet. A row
// with `, 1` takes the header colour (optionmenuitems.zs:592-598), the same
// form the engine uses (`StaticText "$SCALEMNU_OVERRIDE", 1`, menudef.txt).
//
// ONE LANGUAGE ID PER LINE. A StaticText row is one line: it does not wrap
// and a "\n" inside it would draw over the next row. LANGUAGE splits every
// credit into lines of at most 40 characters (tests/test_credits.py), and
// both languages have the same ids in the same order, so this list serves
// both. Credits that a licence obliges are checked against the licence
// registers by that test; the Internationale line is Jerry Engelbach's,
// word for word as docs/sound/MUSIC-RIGHTS.md 4.5 gives it; Peter Gerloff's
// CC0 radio sequences need no credit and get one as a courtesy (ADR 009).
//
// THE DISCLAIMER. "A fan project, not affiliated with id Software" is the
// CEO's (D46). It sits right under the project's name, the first thing the
// screen says, two rows because the sentence is longer than 40 characters.
//
// SCROLLING. The list is longer than one screen at most resolutions. The
// mouse wheel and Page Down scroll a menu with no selectable row
// (OptionMenu.OnUIEvent / MenuEvent, optionmenu.zs:185-206, 343-355); the
// arrow keys move a selection and there is none. The obligatory lines are
// at the top, so they are on the first screen either way. NOT VERIFIED in
// the engine: how many rows the first screen shows, and that a 40-character
// line fits the narrowest clean width (the PM's engine pass, D26).
OptionMenu "SD_CreditsMenu"
{
	Title "$SD_CRED_TITLE"
	StaticText "$SD_CRED_H_TEAM", 1
	StaticText "$SD_CRED_TEAM_1"
	StaticText "$SD_CRED_FAN_1"
	StaticText "$SD_CRED_FAN_2"
	StaticText "$SD_CRED_TEAM_2"
	StaticText "$SD_CRED_TEAM_3"
