// --- Getting there --------------------------------------------------------
// BUG E2, found in-engine 2026-10-13: the mod's screen was attached to
// "OptionsMenu" alone, and the player could not reach it. GZDoom ships TWO
// options screens - the long one ("OptionsMenu", gzdoom.pk3/menudef.txt) and
// a short one for newcomers ("OptionsMenuSimple", gzdoom.pk3/menudef.zsimple)
// - and picks between them at the moment the item is activated:
//
//     case NAME_Optionsmenu:
//         if (m_simpleoptions) menu = NAME_OptionsmenuSimple;
//                       -- gzdoom 4.14.2, src/menu/doommenu.cpp:271
//
// `m_simpleoptions` is archived and defaults to TRUE, so on a fresh install
// "Options" opens the SHORT screen and our entry, appended to the long one,
// was nowhere. The player found it only after turning the simple menu off,
// or through "Full options menu". Both screens therefore get the entry.
//
// This is append, not replace: a protected menu rejects Command and
// SafeCommand from a mod but accepts Submenu, Option and StaticText.
//
// AddOptionMenu on a name the engine does not define is a hard parse error
// ("%s is not an option menu that can be extended", menudef.cpp:1249), so
// both names below are load-bearing: if a future GZDoom drops the simple
// menu, this lump stops loading until the line goes. Debt T13.
//
// `BEFORE "os_Menu"` puts the entry in the MIDDLE of the list instead of
// appending it. Appending looked right and was not: both screens already
// run to the bottom of a 200-line screen, and the new row landed under the
// last visible one - present, reachable by scrolling, and invisible to
// anyone who did not know to scroll (seen in-engine 2026-10-13).
// "os_Menu" is the Option Search entry, which both screens have; the
// engine matches on an item's ACTION, and when it finds no match it
// silently appends instead of failing (GetInsertIndex, menudef.cpp:802),
// so a renamed anchor degrades to the old behaviour rather than breaking.
AddOptionMenu "OptionsMenuSimple" BEFORE "os_Menu"
{
	Submenu "$SD_OPTMNU_TITLE", "SD_OptionsMenu"
	StaticText " "
}

AddOptionMenu "OptionsMenu" BEFORE "os_Menu"
{
	Submenu "$SD_OPTMNU_TITLE", "SD_OptionsMenu"
	StaticText " "
}
